WEBVTT

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:01.819
Do not borrow percentage improvement

00:00:01.819 --> 00:00:04.100
benchmarks from other vendors, and

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:05.640
do not even borrow benchmarks from

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:07.479
other workflows within your own company.

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:09.520
You have to test this system

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:11.960
against your own current manual process

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:13.920
for a highly specific decision.

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:15.499
How do you structure that measurement?

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:17.660
You start with a representative business

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:19.540
question where you already definitively

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:20.980
know the correct answer.

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:23.040
You test whether the new AI

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:24.940
workflow selects the right concepts,

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:27.939
uses the right DAX calculations, strictly

00:00:27.939 --> 00:00:30.460
respects user access permissions, and

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:32.060
returns evidence that a human operator

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:33.199
can actually verify.

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:34.499
And then you time it.

00:00:35.019 --> 00:00:36.440
Then you strictly time how long

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:38.360
that entire process takes, compared

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:39.640
to how long your human analysts

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:42.460
take today. And crucially, you must

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:43.880
include the time it takes the

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:45.880
human operator to rigorously review

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:48.000
and correct the AI's output in

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:48.800
your final calculation.
